sentences.l:
And Hector, from near, standing, urged on Apollo,
like to Phaenops, Asius’-son, who to him of all
guest-friends was dearest, at Abydus in a house dwelling;

for on foot at first, having left the both-sides-curving ships,
he came, and to the Trojans great strength he would have put into their hands,
if Coeranus had not quickly driven the fleet-footed horses;

for close-set javelins
against him dart from bold hands
and burning torches, from which he trembles, hurrying though he is;

“Ajaxes, two leaders of the Argives, and Meriones,
now let someone of the kindness of Patroclus, miserable,
be mindful;
